ENTRYPOINT ["java", "-jar", "app.jar"]


============================================================
5. docker build - BASIC IMAGE BUILD
============================================================

# Build an image using the Dockerfile in the current directory
docker build -t my-app:v1.0 .

# Same command using the long form of --tag
docker build --tag my-app:v1.0 .

Meaning:

docker build
    -> Builds a Docker image.

-t / --tag
    -> Assigns a name and tag to the image.

my-app
    -> Image repository/name.

v1.0
    -> Image tag/version.

.
    -> Build context.
       The current directory is sent to Docker as the build context.

# If no tag is specified, Docker normally uses :latest
docker build -t my-app .

# Equivalent image name:
# my-app:latest


