============================================================
80. IMPORTANT DIFFERENCES
============================================================

docker build
    -> Creates an image from a Dockerfile.

docker run
    -> Creates and starts a new container from an image.

docker start
    -> Starts an existing stopped container.

docker stop
    -> Gracefully stops a running container.

docker restart
    -> Restarts an existing container.

docker kill
    -> Immediately terminates a container.

docker rm
    -> Removes a container.

docker rmi
    -> Removes an image.

docker pull
    -> Downloads an image from a registry.

docker push
    -> Uploads an image to a registry.

docker tag
    -> Creates another tag/reference for an image.

docker exec
    -> Executes a command inside a running container.

docker logs
    -> Displays container output/logs.

docker inspect
    -> Displays detailed metadata.

docker save
    -> Saves an image to a TAR archive.

docker load
    -> Loads an image from a TAR archive.

docker export
    -> Exports a container filesystem.

docker import
    -> Creates an image from an exported filesystem.

docker compose
    -> Manages multi-container applications.

docker buildx
    -> Advanced builds, including multi-platform builds.


