83. BEST PRACTICES
============================================================

# 1. Use small base images when appropriate.
# 2. Use multi-stage Docker builds for compiled applications.
# 3. Use .dockerignore.
# 4. Do not store secrets in Dockerfiles.
# 5. Prefer environment/runtime configuration for deployment settings.
# 6. Avoid running applications as root.
# 7. Use explicit image versions rather than relying only on latest.
# 8. Keep containers focused on one primary responsibility.
# 9. Use health checks for services where appropriate.
# 10. Configure restart policies for appropriate workloads.
# 11. Monitor CPU and memory usage.
# 12. Scan images for vulnerabilities in CI/CD.
# 13. Use immutable/versioned image tags for deployments.
# 14. Use multi-stage builds to reduce final image size.
# 15. Keep Dockerfiles reproducible and version-controlled.
# 16. Do not use docker commit as the normal production build process.
# 17. Clean up unused Docker resources carefully.
# 18. Use Docker Compose for local multi-service development.
# 19. Use Buildx for multi-platform builds.
# 20. Use a private registry for controlled production deployments.


